    "connectEdges": { "kind": "title1", "maxW": 1330, "text": "When connecting doesn't go to plan", "w": 240, "x": 0, "y": 3904 },
    "connectFlow": { "kind": "title1", "maxW": 3210, "text": "Connecting a bank — happy path", "w": 240, "x": 0, "y": 2640 },
    "connectHow": {
      "fill": "teal",
      "text": "Press Play on 04 Connect a bank to click through.\n\nPath: pick provider → see what BACI will and won't access → sign in and approve at the bank → back in BACI, accounts found → tick accounts (live) → sync → connected → connect another bank or Done.\n\nSame flow is reused from Accounts › Add account; there, Done returns to Accounts.\n\nOn the bank screen, Don't allow / Cancel goes to E1. On Syncing, the link under the button previews E2. Accounts › Re-authenticate opens E3.\n\nTweaks: 04b start step, 05a sync progress, E1 failure reason (cancelled / timed out / bank down).\n\n[OPEN BANKING PROVIDER] is a placeholder for the regulated aggregator you choose.",
      "w": 320,
      "x": 3300,
      "y": 2940
    },
    "onboarding": { "kind": "title1", "maxW": 1330, "text": "Onboarding — welcome, consent, profile", "w": 240, "x": 0, "y": -300 },
    "product": { "kind": "title1", "maxW": 2270, "text": "Insight, dashboard, accounts and agent", "w": 240, "x": 0, "y": 1060 },
    "productMore": { "kind": "title1", "maxW": 2740, "text": "Ask BACI, settings and user control", "x": 0, "y": 5168 },
    "flowTitle": { "kind": "title1", "maxW": 2650, "text": "Start here — the whole journey on one page", "x": 3900, "y": -300 },
    "handoff": {
      "fill": "blue",
      "w": 420,
      "x": 3900,
      "y": 1880,
      "text": "Handoff for Claude Code\n\nPress Play on 01 Introduction to click the whole journey: onboarding → connect banks → first insight → Home → Ask BACI → Accounts → Settings.\n\nThe build spec lives in the repo at docs/design/BACI_FLOW_SPEC.md, with CLAUDE.md at the root pointing to it. Every artboard ID here (01…10, 04a–05b, E1–E3, A1–A2, S1–S4) is a section in that spec with its route, API calls, states, transitions and acceptance checks. The artboard sources are copied to docs/design/screens/."
    },
